I added branch-prediction hints so the common standard-field fallback path falls through without taken branches, while preserving the original checks and return values. The profile pointer is also loaded once to avoid redundant member access.

```cpp
FIT_UINT8 Field::GetType() const
{
    if (__builtin_expect(type != FIT_UINT8_INVALID, 0))
        return type;

    const Profile* p = profile;
    if (__builtin_expect(p == NULL, 0))
        return FIT_UINT8_INVALID;

    const FIT_UINT8 index = profileIndex;
    if (__builtin_expect(index >= p->numFields, 0))
        return FIT_UINT8_INVALID;

    return p->fields[index].type;
}
```